=== parameters ===
enter z< -2.0 exit z>= 0.0 stop 0.03
look-ahead rule: z[t] may only change position from t+1 onward (asserted)
cite: Stern Dhar counter-trend; Canvas m7; OU/AR(1) half-life for lookback choice
further_reading: Ernest P. Chan, Algorithmic Trading: Winning Strategies and Their Rationale, Wiley 2013 (ISBN 978-1-118-46014-6) — no quotes

=== AR(1) / OU half-life ===
model: dx = a + b * x_{t-1} + eps
OU link: kappa ≈ -ln(1+b) per bar; half_life = ln(2)/kappa = -ln(2)/ln(1+b)
a=0.932778 b=-0.012340 kappa=0.012417
half_life_bars=55.82 n=299
rule: z_lookback ≈ 1.5 * HL → Z_LB=60; holding_hint ≈ 1 * HL → 40 bars
teach: if HL is very large (near unit root), fade strategies are slow/fragile
ASSERT_z_exit_no_lookahead: OK (z[t] changes position only from t+1)
stop_exits=4

